Article 18
The policy for protection and fulfillment of children's rights in the health sector is as follows:
a. providing free health services for children from poor families;
b. organizing comprehensive health efforts for children;
c. ensuring that infants receive exclusive breast milk from their mothers;
d. ensuring that children receive nutrition that meets standards;
e. protecting children from attempts to transplant their body organs to other parties; and
f. ensuring the provision of growth and development monitoring for toddlers and pre-school age children.

Article 38
(1) The Regional Government, in efforts to provide special protection for children, is responsible for:
a. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of special protection for children;
b. providing access to public services and social services for children with disabilities;
c. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for special protection for children;
d. cooperating with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of special protection for children in accordance with the laws and regulations;
e. carrying out rehabilitation and assistance for children who become victims of acts of violence;
f. providing special protection to children in emergency situations, children in conflict with the law, children who are victims of acts of violence and trafficking in persons, children from minority and isolated groups, children exploited economically and/or sexually, children who are victims of abuse of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and HIV/AIDS;
g. providing inclusive education for children with special needs; and
h. taking preventive actions in order to prevent violations of children's rights.
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to provide special protection for children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by the regional apparatus that implements government affairs under its authority in the social sector.

Article 12
(1) Regional Government in the context of fulfillment of children's rights is responsible for:
a. establishing and implementing policies, programs, and activities for the fulfillment of children's rights;
b. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of fulfillment of children's rights;
c. conducting guidance and supervision in the context of implementation of fulfillment of children's rights;
d. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, group, gender, ethnic group, culture and language, legal status of the child, birth order of the child, and physical and/or mental condition; and
e. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or non-governmental organizations in the implementation of fulfillment of children's rights.
(2) Regional Government in the context of fulfillment of children's rights may cooperate with the community, business sector, and mass media.
(3) The responsibility of Regional Government in efforts to fulfill children's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

